{
  "description": "core §8.6, reading a deployment catalog. Written by hand from the text, checked, never blessed. Each case is a catalog's `text` → `expect`: `{\"id\": …}`, the 8 hex digits of an accepted catalog's id (ids.json says how it is computed), or `{\"refused\": token}`, the first refusal in §8.6's order: `json` (not strict JSON: RFC 8259, no member twice in one object), `format` (not an object whose `format` is the string `zk2-catalog/1`), `member` (at the top level, `epoch` or `entries` missing, or a member besides `format`, `epoch`, `entries` and `lineage`), `epoch` (not an integer from 0 to 2^53 - 1), `entries` (not an array of objects, or more than 1,024 of them); then, for each entry in order, `member` (not exactly `index`, `iface` and `contract`), `index` (not the integer of its position), `iface` (not a string holding an interface id, core §1.2), `contract` (not a string holding a fingerprint), `duplicate` (an earlier entry's pair); then `lineage` (present and not a non-empty array of objects); then, for each lineage item in order, `member` (not exactly `id` and `entries`) and `lineage` (an `id` not 8 lowercase hex digits, or an earlier item's or the catalog's own; an `entries` not an integer, below the item before it's, or above the catalog's count). An integer is a JSON number written as digits alone, with no sign, fraction or exponent. A catalog whose own id is one of its lineage's needs a 32-bit collision, so no case holds one.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "note": "the smallest catalog: an epoch of 0 and no entries",
      "text": "{\"format\": \"zk2-catalog/1\", \"epoch\": 0, \"entries\": []}",
      "expect": {
        "id": "7e895b70"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "§8.6's example, without its lineage: three revisions",
      "text": "{\n  \"format\": \"zk2-catalog/1\",\n  \"epoch\": 1767225600,\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"index\": 0,\n      \"iface\": \"modem.v3\",\n      \"contract\": \"sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"iface\": \"config.v1\",\n      \"contract\": \"sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"index\": 2,\n      \"iface\": \"health.v1\",\n      \"contract\": \"sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "expect": {
        "id": "0a90fd61"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "a successor: its lineage names the catalog of two entries it extends",
      "text": "{\"format\": \"zk2-catalog/1\", \"epoch\": 1767225600, \"entries\": [{\"index\": 0, \"iface\": \"modem.v3\", \"contract\": \"sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953\"}, {\"index\": 1, \"iface\": \"config.v1\", \"contract\": \"sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1\"}, {\"index\": 2, \"iface\": \"health.v1\", \"contract\": \"sha256:e9dbcdcb2fc325ca3121fdcacf7badd0091f62d97ab4c7d7a5f022dd8d6671df\"}], \"lineage\": [{\"id\": \"eddb48d5\", \"entries\": 2}]}",
      "expect": {
        "id": "0319128a"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "one interface at two revisions, each its own pair",
      "text": "{\"format\": \"zk2-catalog/1\", \"epoch\": 1767225600, \"entries\": [{\"index\": 0, \"iface\": \"modem.v3\", \"contract\": \"sha256:9a3e2859a538a95daafc53e7dffe8c9d0610312f7650f27250b9e6fee0965953\"}, {\"index\": 1, \"iface\": \"config.v1\", \"contract\": \"sha256:727ff0090b99ad8fc09b5398804d1a14288bebf661f374ec6904351344a1a7b1\"}, {\"index\": 2, \"iface\": \"modem.v3\", \"contract\": \"sha256:ea38eab240a4b114b9309b814afad4e77fcda547047fb9d94c062055c6acf119\"}]}",
